About Wing:&nbsp;

Wing offers drone delivery as a safe, fast, and sustainable solution for last mile logistics. Consumer appetites for on-demand services are increasing, but current delivery methods are inefficient, costly, and contribute to road accidents and air pollution. Wing’s fleet of highly automated delivery drones can transport small packages directly from businesses to homes on-demand, in minutes. We design, build, and operate our aircraft, and offer drone delivery services on two continents. Our technology is designed to be easy to integrate into existing delivery and logistics networks, offering a scalable drone delivery solution for a broad range of businesses. Wing is a part of Google's parent company, Alphabet, and our mission is to create the preferred means of delivery for the planet. If you're ready to do the greatest work of your life, come join us.

About the Role:

Wing is looking for a Sourcing Lead, Direct to join our Sourcing team. This role is onsite based in Palo Alto, CA . You will lead the strategy for our hardware supply chain design, build and develop our team of global sourcing managers and enable Wing’s growth by partnering closely with engineering, operations, legal and finance teams. Your leadership across both the direct team, our suppliers, and with cross-functional stakeholder partners will ensure that the hardware supporting Wing’s services can be built cost-effectively at scale, meet quality and compliance standards, and are delivered on time.

Our team moves fast and we will look to you to learn quickly, lead with conviction and build strong relationships both internally and externally. This is a role with high impact and high influence, spanning many cross functional teams and work-streams across engineering, legal, finance, quality, manufacturing, product management and more. You are equally comfortable in deep dive technical conversations around new product design as you are at our partner factories, scaling mass production. Most importantly, you consider the team’s success your success, and you are genuinely excited about enabling the growth and development of your team members.&nbsp;

What You’ll Do:&nbsp;

• Lead commercial engagement and sourcing strategy for our full hardware supply chain across both aircraft and ground infrastructure&nbsp;

• Critically evaluate our current supplier portfolio and create a long term strategy for each commodity &amp; technology to support Wing’s innovation roadmap

• Mentor, coach and close the negotiations to secure best contractual terms and pricing for our supplier partnerships

• Partner closely with internal cross-functional teams, our suppliers and our contract manufacturers to ensure quality and manufacturability of our assemblies&nbsp;

• Partner closely with our engineering and other technical teams to drive the right partner selection for design and development from concept through mass production

• Create the strategy and apply the playbook across all our hardware for new supplier market research, qualification and industrialization&nbsp;

• Assess and mitigate long term supply chain risk, especially in regulated markets&nbsp;

• Mentor and coach the team in developing successful, long-term supplier relationships globally

• Build trust and lightweight, yet scalable processes with all cross functional teams

What You’ll Need:&nbsp;

• 12+ years of experience developing and managing global supplier relationships and bringing high-volume products from concept to mass production&nbsp;

• 5+ years of directly managing global supply chain teams&nbsp;

• A Bachelor's Degree in a technical field (e.g., mechanical, industrial, or electrical engineering) is preferred, but equivalent practical experience in supply chain, manufacturing, military service, or consulting will also be considered

• Ability to have hard conversations with peers, direct reports and partners while preserving trust and relationships&nbsp;

